From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:36:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] xobject.cc: no inline values for dynamically created
 types on 3.13+

dt.Type is created at runtime by calling type() and then widening
tp_basicsize to hold the C++ object. Since Python 3.13 such a heap
type gets Py_TPFLAGS_INLINE_VALUES, and on 3.13 the inline values are
always located directly after the PyObject header, i.e. on top of the
C++ fields. The garbage collector then reads those fields as object
pointers, and the interpreter crashes in subtype_traverse() on the
first collection after `import datatable`:

  Fatal Python error: Segmentation fault
  Current thread ... (most recent call first):
    Garbage-collecting

Clear the flag after creating the type, so that the instance dict (if
ever needed) is kept out of line, as it is on Python <= 3.12. 3.14
places the inline values after tp_basicsize instead, but there is no
benefit in keeping them for these types.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [upstream has merged no external code change since the 1.1.0 release]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 src/core/python/xobject.cc | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/python/xobject.cc b/src/core/python/xobject.cc
index 6b212f9..783796c 100644
--- a/src/core/python/xobject.cc
+++ b/src/core/python/xobject.cc
@@ -82,6 +82,11 @@ void XTypeMaker::initialize_type() {
     });
     type = reinterpret_cast<PyTypeObject*>(std::move(typeObj).release());
     type->tp_basicsize = static_cast<Py_ssize_t>(object_size);
+    #ifdef Py_TPFLAGS_INLINE_VALUES
+      // Inline values live right after the object header, where the
+      // C++ fields of the object are stored instead
+      type->tp_flags &= ~Py_TPFLAGS_INLINE_VALUES;
+    #endif
   }
   else {
     type = new PyTypeObject;
-- 
